issue.body:
I believe that all interfaces: Answer1, Answer2 and so on have bad code example in javadoc.

For example Answer1 has this: 

`   when(mock.someMethod(anyString())).thenAnswer(new Answer<Integer, String>() {
       Integer answer(String arg) {
           return arg.length();
       }
   });`

which does not compile. 
First: Answer1 should be there instead of Answer 
Second: thenAnswer method does not accept Answer1 

BTW. I personally consider naming classes or interfaces with digits as last character as poorly named construct. 
I know that there is a "fashion" right now to give names like in some functional languages, but still bothers me as something that is not aesthetic at all. Just a thought.
